WEBVTT

00:00:00.250 --> 00:00:04.571
Once the award is out, log it in your logbook — which line you got.

00:00:04.571 --> 00:00:07.796
After you've flown the month, tell it how it went.

00:00:07.796 --> 00:00:14.440
Over the months it adds up to what you've held, where you've been, and where your seniority's heading —

00:00:14.440 --> 00:00:16.439
and it helps your next ranking.

00:00:17.139 --> 00:00:20.683
You can choose to share your award with other pilots.

00:00:20.683 --> 00:00:27.769
It shows only your seniority number, never your name or employee number, and you can withdraw it any time.

00:00:27.769 --> 00:00:33.986
Shared awards are what make "Your chances" and "what pilots held" more accurate for everyone.

00:00:34.686 --> 00:00:39.220
Signed in with your own pack, you can also subscribe in your calendar.

00:00:39.220 --> 00:00:43.042
Make your link once and add it to Apple, Google or Outlook.

00:00:43.042 --> 00:00:51.462
The trips on your top line show up on their own and stay up to date, and once you log your award, the calendar shows that instead.

